Sonochemical synthesis of Nano TMU-46, 47 and 48 under ultrasonic irradiation   
To prepare Nano TMU-46,47 and 48, 0.201 g of Cu $\mathrm{(CH_{3}C O O)_{2}\bullet H_{2}O}$ (1 mmol), $0.258\ \mathrm{g}$ of oba (1 mmol) and $0.318\mathrm{~g~}$ of synthesized amide ligands bpfb (1 mmol), $0.318\ \mathrm{g}$ of bpta (1 mmol), and 0.368 $\mathrm{{g}(1\ m m o l)}$ of bpfn were dissolved in $15~\mathrm{ml}$ of $\mathrm{N,N^{\prime}}$ -Dimethylformamide (DMF) respectively. The mixture was positioned in a high-density ultrasonic probe and sonicated for 60 min at ambient temperature, operating with a power output of $18~\mathrm{W}$ . The sonicator used in this study was a Misonix Sonicator 3000 with an adjustable power output (maximum $600\mathrm{W}$ at $50/60\mathrm{kHz}$ ). A horn type tube Pyrex reactor was custom-made and fitted to the sonicator bar.  After filtering and washing with DMF the result precipitates were dried in air. (Fig.1)   
